    "result_text": "All tests pass. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature for `POST /api/owners`, following the OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo.\n\n**Behavior:** When a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the owner is allowed at an address already used by a same-last-name owner (the existing `EnsureUniqueHousehold` check already skips rejection in that case), and now every owner in that household is assigned the same stable `householdId`, which is returned on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`AssignHousehold.java`** (new function) \u2014 the core logic. For a `sharesHousehold` request it finds existing owners with the same normalized last name + address, derives a stable `householdId` deterministically (`HH-` + SHA-256 prefix of normalized lastName|address), reuses an id already held by a member for stability, sets it on the new owner, and back-fills any existing members that lack one \u2014 so \"both\" ends of the household carry the same id.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignHousehold` step into the pipeline (after `ensureUniqueHousehold`, before `assignCustomerCode`), under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `householdId` field (`@Column(name = \"household_id\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it by name.\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `household_id` column to `owners` in hsqldb, h2, mysql, and postgres schema files (tests run on hsqldb).\n\n**Result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId` acceptance test passes: two owners joining an existing owner's household both receive the same non-blank `householdId`.",
